  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...No significant weather concerns this week.\n\nHigh pressure centered over the Province of Ontario, north of \nthe Great Lakes and south of Hudson Bay, will build east tonight\nand will be centered over New England on Wednesday. The high \nthen moves offshore into the western Atlantic as the week \nprogresses. A weak cold front passes through the region Friday, \nand then high pressure returns for the weekend. Low pressure may\napproach the region for the start of next week.\n\nWith high pressure settling north of the area tonight, \nexcellent radiational cooling conditions set up with clear skies\nand light winds. Will opt for the colder NBM10 guidance for low\ntemperatures in the 30s to low 40s. Not expecting frost or \nfreeze conditions where the growing season is still in effect. \n\nOtherwise, dry conditions through Saturday with high \ntemperatures generally from the mid and upper 60s on Wednesday \nto the mid 70s or so by Friday. Cooler, but still slightly above\nnormal temperatures expected for this weekend. Rain may arrive \non Sunday or Monday depending on the timing, strength, and \nplacement of that aforementioned low pressure system.",
